Credits

No third-party code is included. The driver works with "PiPup - TV Notifications" by
Alexander Savin (Google Play: nyc.savin.pipup; https://pipup.android.savin.nyc), a fork of
PiPup by rogro82. The requests to it follow PiPup's "How to use" page
(https://pipup.android.savin.nyc/how-to-use.html) and its maker's Home Assistant
integration (https://github.com/alex-savin/hassio-integration-pipup-notification, MIT
License); no code was copied from them.

Finding TVs (SSDP) follows Snap One's SSDP module as DirectorLink uses it
(https://github.directorlink.io, Apache License 2.0). Control4 interfaces follow the public
Snap One DriverWorks documentation (https://snap-one.github.io/docs-driverworks-fundamentals/).

The test fixtures in tests/ describe a made-up home; names, addresses, tokens and ids in them
are invented, except PiPup's answers, which follow what PiPup 0.3.4 answered on a real TV.
